#problem[Prove that for all $n gt.eq 2$ the set $S_n $ is generated by the elements $cyc(1,2) "and" cyc(1,2,dots,n)$  ][

Consider that $ cyc(1,2,dots,n) cyc(1,2) cyc(1,2,dots,n)^(-1) &= cyc(2,3) \ cyc(1,2,dots,n)cyc(2,3)cyc(1,2,dots,n)^(-1)&=cyc(3,4) \ &dots.v \ cyc(1,2,dots,n)cyc(n-2,n-1)cyc(1,2,dots,n)^(-1) &= cyc(i,i+1) $ for $1 lt.eq i lt.eq n-1$

By problem 4, we know that each $sigma in S_n$ can be written as a product of elements of the form $cyc(i,i+1)$

Since $cyc(1,2)$ and $cyc(1,2,dots,n)$ generates such elements, they also generate $S_n$

$qed$ 
  
]
